## Signal Density Optimization (AI-Leverage)

> **Maximize signal density before Opus. Ground factor: (load-bearing facts) ÷ (time cost).**

### Model Role Specialization
- **Cheap models (Kimi/Haiku/Local):** Discovery and extraction only — read docs, scan code, extract patterns
- **Opus:** Synthesis and decision only — structure sprint docs, decide scope sequence
- **Never feed raw research to Opus** — always `/compress` first (10× token reduction, identical quality)

### Compression Rules
- No prose, no explanation — only verified facts
- Token names must be component classes from `addComponents`, not utilities
- File paths must exist (verified in codebase)
- GROQ shapes from live queries only
- Maximum Opus input for sprint generation: **1000 tokens**

### Load-Bearing Fact Definition
Any fact that, if missing or wrong, would cause the sprint doc to drift or the executor model to fail.

