## Opus Sprint Specification Quality (Universal)

When generating sprint specs with Opus, output MUST include:

### 1. Gap Coverage Mapping
- Every SC explicitly references audit gaps (G1, G2, G3...)
- Traceability: Audit finding → Spec → Implementation

### 2. Line-Number Precision
- Exact file paths with line numbers/ranges
- Exact class names for before/after states

### 3. Constraint-First Architecture
- Scope Lock Rules section FIRST (what NOT to touch)
- Anti-patterns section with explicit DON'Ts

### 4. Layer-Based Sequencing
- Pass 1: Skeleton (semantic HTML)
- Pass 2: Data (real data integration)
- Pass 3: Build (Structure → Layout → Surface → Interaction)

### 5. Verifiable DoDs
- Build gate after EVERY SC
- Objective pass/fail criteria only
- No subjective "looks good" requirements

### 6. Functional Grouping
- Group A: Foundation (layout, structure)
- Group B: Core UX (product display)
- Group C: Functional systems (filters)
- Group D: Polish (skeletons, semantics)

**Reference:** `_project/lessons/workflows/opus-sprint-specification-generation.md`

